 "purpose": "The layout of the panel screens: which panel goes where, by screen size (werk/schermen.md).",
 "details": "One place for all sizes so no screen counts columns itself: from 80x24 the panels grow to 120x40; on a bigger screen (such as a tty of 240x67) the block stays that size and sits in the middle. The series bar is on top (a panel from 30 rows, else one line), Question, Tip and cheat sheet on the left, the klad beside them where a klad exists, the buddy on the right; with the clock window open the buddy's column stays empty. Rows 0 (breadcrumb) and h-1 (key bar) belong to the whole screen.",
